The output of SEL RTAC project export parsing changed. The tag tables of a device (e.g. ``binary_inputs``, ``coils`` and ``holding_registers`` in ``extra.Devices``) now have all of the columns of the table, with the column names from the export as keys (e.g. ``Enable``, ``Tag Type``, ``Point Number``, ``Register Address Start``), instead of the keys ``enable``, ``type``, ``point``, ``address``, ``register_start`` and the misspelled ``regsiter_stop``. Every other setting page of a device is also included. In ``peat.modules.sel.rtac_parse``, the functions ``parse_device_io_tags``, ``parse_device_coils``, ``parse_device_discrete_inputs`` and ``parse_device_modbus_registers`` were replaced by ``parse_setting_page`` and ``parse_setting_pages``, and ``parse_settings`` now returns all of the settings on the "Settings" page (it no longer takes a list of settings).
